The brand gradient is:

```
linear-gradient(135deg, #10E66A 0%, #12C679 28%, #188AAC 66%, #197DB4 100%)
```

These are mapped to Tailwind tokens in `src/app/globals.css` via the
`@theme inline` block (e.g. `bg-brand-gradient`, `text-brand-teal`,
`bg-surface-tint`, `border-line`).

## 3. No dark theme rule

- The site must never switch to a dark theme.
- `color-scheme: light` is set on `:root` in `globals.css`.
- Do not introduce `dark:` Tailwind variants.

## 4. Logo usage rules

Official assets belong in `public/brand/` (see
[`public/brand/README.md`](../public/brand/README.md)).

- Use the **horizontal** logo in the header and footer.
- Use the **icon/avatar** version for favicon, small badges, social preview,
  and compact UI.
- Prefer transparent / white-background variants.
- **Do not** use the black-background logo variant in the main UI.
- **Do not** distort, recolor, stretch, or crop the logo.

Placeholder on-brand SVGs are checked in at:

- `public/brand/taskcover-horizontal.svg`
- `public/brand/taskcover-icon.svg`
- `public/brand/og-default.svg`

Replace each file with the official asset (same filename) when provided.

## 5. Gradient usage rules

Use the Taskcover gradient in a **controlled, premium** way:

- CTA fills and borders
- Hero dashboard glow
- Small section accents (eyebrow dot, timeline line)
- Data visualization highlights
- Card emphasis (sparingly)
- Badges and icon tiles
- Charts (Recharts strokes / fills)

Do **not** overuse the gradient:

- No rainbow gradients.
- No neon-heavy design.
- No colorful clutter.
- Most surfaces remain white and clean.

Helper utilities live in `globals.css`:

- `.bg-brand-gradient`
- `.bg-brand-gradient-soft`
- `.text-brand-gradient`
- `.ring-brand-glow`
- `.bg-dot-grid`
- `.bg-line-grid`

## 6. UI component style

- Rounded surfaces (`rounded-xl`, `rounded-2xl`, `rounded-3xl`).
- Subtle borders (`border-line`, `border-line-soft`).
- Soft shadows, never heavy drop shadows.
- Generous whitespace; consistent section rhythm (`Section` component).
- Mobile-first responsive grids.
- One clear H1 per page; subsequent sections use `SectionHeader` (H2).

## 7. Motion rules

- Motion must support comprehension, not distract.
- Prefer subtle transitions (`duration-200`, `duration-300`).
- Accordion open/close uses CSS keyframes defined in `globals.css`.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` where animations are added later.
- No parallax-for-parallax-sake; no flashing or strobing.

## 8. Accessibility rules

- WCAG AA contrast minimums for text on backgrounds.
- Visible focus rings using brand teal (`:focus-visible` rule in `globals.css`).
- All interactive elements are keyboard reachable.
- Icons paired with text labels or `aria-label`s; decorative icons use
  `aria-hidden="true"`.
- Semantic landmarks: `header`, `main`, `nav` (with `aria-label`), `footer`.
- Section headings linked via `aria-labelledby` where appropriate.